🧩 What is a List?
Ordered collection of elements.

Allows duplicates.

Elements can be accessed by index.

✅ Example:
java
Copy
Edit
List<String> names = new ArrayList<>();
names.add("Ali");
names.add("Ali");  // Duplicate allowed
System.out.println(names.get(0));  // Ali
🧩 What is a Set?
Unordered collection of unique elements.

Duplicates not allowed.

Does not support indexing.

✅ Example:
java
Copy
Edit
Set<String> names = new HashSet<>();
names.add("Ali");
names.add("Ali");  // Duplicate ignored
System.out.println(names.size());  // 1


🔍 Set vs List – Key Differences
| Feature          | **List**                      | **Set**                                                                                    |
| ---------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Order**        | Maintains **insertion order** | ❌ No guaranteed order (`HashSet`)<br>✅ Ordered in `LinkedHashSet`<br>✅ Sorted in `TreeSet` |
| **Duplicates**   | ✅ Allowed                     | ❌ Not allowed                                                                              |
| **Index-based**  | ✅ Yes (`list.get(0)`)         | ❌ No                                                                                       |
| **Performance**  | Slower lookup (`O(n)`)        | Faster lookup (`O(1)` for `HashSet`)                                                       |
| **Common Types** | `ArrayList`, `LinkedList`     | `HashSet`, `LinkedHashSet`, `TreeSet`                                                      |


🚀 When to Use What?
| Use Case                                 | Use **List** | Use **Set**           |
| ---------------------------------------- | ------------ | --------------------- |
| Need duplicates                          | ✅ Yes        | ❌ No                  |
| Access by index                          | ✅ Yes        | ❌ No                  |
| Fast lookups & uniqueness                | ❌ No         | ✅ Yes                 |
| Maintain insertion order with uniqueness | ❌ No         | ✅ Use `LinkedHashSet` |
| Need sorted data                         | ❌ No         | ✅ Use `TreeSet`       |

